Each term contains the common factor \(10^{2000}>0\). Dividing both the numerator and denominator by it removes the large powers:
\[
\begin{aligned}
\frac{10^{2000}+10^{2002}}{10^{2001}+10^{2001}}
&=\frac{1+100}{10+10}\\
&=\frac{101}{20}=5.05.
\end{aligned}
\]
This is only \(0.05\) away from \(5\), while every other listed choice is at least \(4.05\) away. The closest number is \(\boxed{5}\), choice \(\mathrm{D}\).
